        "permissionRule": null,
        "helperInfo": "Description: A global system configuration saving mode, the mode decides how and when to save running configuration into the persistent configuration. System requests all running configuration are saved into persistent configuration before config-saving-mode switching. Available Value: - \"manual\": The system work in manual config saving mode. In this mode, the user input configuration won’t be saved into persistent configuration along automatically with it activate in running configuration. The running configuration need be saved into persistent configuration by the manual command. Without manual saving, the system will load the persistent configuration after cold reboot or power cycle. The different between previous running configuration and persistent configuration will change to value of persistent configuration. - \"auto\": The system work in auto config saving mode. The running configuration will be triggered to save into persistent configuration when input configuration activates in running configuration. After system reboot or power cycle the configuration will be kept. default Value: \"manual\"",
